// How the menus look.
//
// The splash, Main Menu and loading screens. Deliberately NOT the sky: the menus are not
// in the world, and they used to borrow the sky's horizon colour only because the
// lighting file happened to load before them. Now that each scenario brings its own
// lighting, that would have meant the menu changing colour depending on which map you
// last played.
//
// Colours are (r, g, b) in sRGB, each 0.0-1.0 — the same form as everywhere else.
(
    // Flat colour behind the menu screens.
    //
    // Dark and desaturated so the white text and the pale button highlights carry the
    // screen. A bright background here fights the buttons, which are drawn as low-alpha
    // white and need something dim to sit on.
    //
    // Changing this does not affect the sky. `lighting.ron` owns that.
    background: (0.10, 0.11, 0.14),
)
